---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "Malaysia eVISA for Pakistanis: Official Application Guide",
  "description": "Use Malaysian Immigration’s current visa requirements and official eVISA portal; distinguish visa approval from arrival formalities and permitted stay.",
  "intro": "Use Malaysian Immigration’s current visa requirements and official eVISA portal; distinguish visa approval from arrival formalities and permitted stay.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Immigration nationality requirements",
      "url": "https://www.imi.gov.my/index.php/en/main-services/visa/visa-requirement-by-country/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Official eVISA portal",
      "url": "https://malaysiavisa.imi.gov.my/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Immigration eVISA FAQ",
      "url": "https://www.imi.gov.my/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/FAQ-PERTANYAAN-eVISA-14.10.2022.pdf"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Check the nationality requirement",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Pakistan appears on Immigration’s visa-required list. Identify the current category for your purpose and residence. A neighbouring country’s exemption or visa-on-arrival arrangement does not automatically apply to a Pakistani passport."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Use the official service",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Begin at malaysiavisa.imi.gov.my and read the displayed requirements before paying. eNTRI is not presented here as a verified current option for Pakistanis. Immigration’s arrival-visa FAQ does not establish Pakistani eligibility; do not build a trip around that assumption."
      ],
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "heading": "Prepare the application",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Follow the live checklist for passport, photo, travel, accommodation and supporting evidence. Use legible scans and matching identity details. If visiting a host, explain the relationship and accommodation consistently.",
        "Compare dates across flights, nights of accommodation and onward plans before submission. Keep the submitted material, payment receipt and application reference together. Provide any requested additional documents through the authorised service."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check fees and result",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Use the fee shown for your case, separating visa and processing charges. The former USD 50 estimate is not a universal current fee. Extra evidence or an interview can add time. Verify the issued eVISA and follow instructions for carrying it."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Keep arrival and stay separate",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A visa does not guarantee entry, and an arrival form does not replace a required visa. Recheck current arrival formalities before departure. Follow the permission at entry; do not assume an automatic 30-day extension or that every transit itinerary removes visa requirements."
      ],
      "source": 0
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
